---
import '../styles/bill-planner.css';
import {months} from '../lib/bill-planner.mjs';
---
<section class="page-shell bp" id="bill-planner">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="bp-intro">
<a class="text-link" href="/resources/">All free resources</a>
<p class="eyebrow">Free worksheet · Financial literacy</p>
<h1>Put your next three bills on one page</h1>
<p class="bp-lead">In 15 minutes, write down three bills, when they’re due and when you plan to pay them. You’ll finish with a simple calendar and one thing to check next.</p>
<p>Use paper or our free worksheet. No signup needed. Keep your financial details private.</p>
</div>
  <div class="bp-work">
    <p class="bp-privacy">Your entries stay in this page. Refreshing or closing clears them. Print or save a copy to keep it. Use short labels; leave out account numbers and passwords.</p>
    <div class="bp-toolbar" id="example">
<button class="btn btn-ghost" id="bp-example" type="button">Try a fictional example</button>
<a class="text-link" href="#print">Print a blank worksheet</a>
<a class="text-link" href="/resources/month-ahead/">Read the walkthrough</a>
</div>
    <div id="bp-replace" class="bp-notice" hidden>
<p>This replaces your entries with a fictional example. Print your work first if you want to keep it.</p>
<button type="button" class="btn btn-red" id="bp-confirm-example">Replace with example</button> <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="bp-cancel-example">Keep my entries</button>
</div>
    <p id="bp-status" role="status">
</p>
    <form id="bp-form" autocomplete="off">
<div class="bp-section-head">
<h2>1. Add three bills</h2>
<div class="bp-month">
<label>Month<select id="bp-month">{months.map((m,i)=>
<option value={i}>{m}</option>)}</select>
</label>
<label>Year<input id="bp-year" type="number" min="1900" max="9999" step="1" aria-describedby="bp-year-error" />
</label>
</div>
</div>
<p id="bp-year-error" class="bp-warning" hidden>Choose a year from 1900 to 9999. The calendar keeps the last valid month.</p>
    <p class="bp-help">
<strong>Due by</strong> is the biller’s deadline. <strong>Pay / withdrawal on</strong> is when you plan to send money or expect an automatic withdrawal. Check processing time with your biller. Leave unknown dates blank.</p>
    <div class="bp-bills">{[0,1,2].map(i=>
<fieldset class="bp-bill">
<legend>Bill {i+1}</legend>
<label>Short bill label<input id={`bp-label-${i}`} maxlength="48" placeholder={['Phone','Electricity','Internet'][i]} />
</label>
<label>Amount in USD (optional)<input id={`bp-amount-${i}`} inputmode="decimal" maxlength="12" placeholder="Leave blank if unknown" aria-describedby={`bp-warning-${i}`} />
</label>
<div class="bp-pair">
<label>Due by<input id={`bp-due-${i}`} type="date" min="1900-01-01" max="9999-12-31" />
</label>
<label>Pay / withdrawal on<input id={`bp-planned-${i}`} type="date" min="1900-01-01" max="9999-12-31" />
</label>
</div>
<div class="bp-pair">
<label>Details are<select id={`bp-certainty-${i}`}>
<option value="check">To check</option>
<option value="estimate">An estimate</option>
<option value="confirmed">Checked by me</option>
</select>
</label>
<label>Payment method<select id={`bp-method-${i}`}>
<option value="check">To check</option>
<option value="manual">Manual</option>
<option value="automatic">Automatic withdrawal</option>
</select>
</label>
</div>
<label>Note (optional)<input id={`bp-notes-${i}`} maxlength="100" placeholder="One thing to remember" />
</label>
<p class="bp-warning" id={`bp-warning-${i}`}>
</p>
</fieldset>)}</div>
    <div class="bp-next">
<h2>2. Choose one thing to check</h2>
<div class="bp-next-grid">
<label>I will check<input id="bp-followup" maxlength="120" placeholder="For example: the electricity amount" />
</label>
<label>Where or with whom<input id="bp-source" maxlength="100" placeholder="For example: the biller’s statement" />
</label>
<label>By this date<input id="bp-when" type="date" min="1900-01-01" max="9999-12-31" />
</label>
</div>
</div>
</form>
    <section class="bp-results" aria-labelledby="bp-result-title">
<div class="bp-section-head">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Your simple calendar</p>
<h2 id="bp-result-title">Your month</h2>
</div>
<div class="bp-toolbar">
<button id="bp-list-view" type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" aria-pressed="true">List</button>
<button id="bp-calendar-view" type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" aria-pressed="false">Calendar</button>
</div>
</div>
<p id="bp-example-notice" class="bp-notice" hidden>Fictional example — all names, amounts and dates are invented. Edits are labeled separately; clear it to start your own worksheet.</p>
<p id="bp-total">
</p>
<p class="bp-help">Only valid entered amounts are totaled, including estimates and unchecked amounts. Missing or invalid amounts are excluded. This partial list is not a full budget, money available to spend or an affordability check. A calendar entry does not make a payment.</p>
<div id="bp-list">
</div>
<div id="bp-calendar" hidden>
</div>
<div id="bp-next-result">
</div>
</section>
    <section class="bp-print-actions" id="print">
<h2>3. Keep your page</h2>
<p>Review a clean worksheet, then use your device’s print dialog to print or save as PDF. A saved PDF is a snapshot, not an editable form. Keep your copy private.</p>
<div class="bp-toolbar">
<button id="bp-print-completed" class="btn btn-red" type="button">Preview my worksheet</button>
<button id="bp-print-blank" class="btn btn-ghost" type="button">Preview blank worksheet</button>
<button id="bp-reset" class="btn btn-ghost" type="button">Clear entries</button>
</div>
</section>
    <div id="bp-clear-confirm" class="bp-notice" hidden>
<p>Clear all entries? Print your work first if you want to keep a copy.</p>
<button id="bp-confirm-reset" type="button" class="btn btn-red">Clear all entries</button> <button id="bp-cancel-reset" type="button" class="btn btn-ghost">Keep my entries</button>
</div>
    <details class="bp-source">
<summary>About this resource &amp; sources</summary>
<p>General education only. Independently prepared by Approaching Infinity, informed by the CFPB’s <a class="text-link" href="https://files.consumerfinance.gov/f/documents/cfpb_your-money-your-goals_bill_calendar_tool_2018-11_ADA.pdf">Your Money, Your Goals bill-calendar tool</a>. This is not the official CFPB worksheet and is not CFPB-approved or endorsed.</p>
</details>
    <noscript>
<p>This fillable planner needs JavaScript. Use the <a class="text-link" href="/resources/month-ahead/">walkthrough’s example</a> with paper, or enable JavaScript for a blank printable worksheet.</p>
</noscript>
  </div>
  <div class="bp-preview-controls" hidden>
<h2 id="bp-preview-title">Worksheet preview</h2>
<p>Review this copy before opening your device’s print dialog.</p>
<div class="bp-toolbar">
<button id="bp-back" class="btn btn-ghost" type="button">Back to worksheet</button>
<button id="bp-open-print" class="btn btn-red" type="button">Print / save as PDF</button>
</div>
</div>
  <article id="bp-print-sheet" class="bp-print-sheet" aria-label="Printable worksheet">
</article>
</div>
</section>
<script>import '../scripts/bill-planner.mjs';</script>
